              <div align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="5" align="center"><b>A 
                breath of fresh air with MSNBC's Donahue!</b></font></div>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="2"> 
              <div align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><a href="http://www.msnbc.com/news/donahue_front.asp" class="dead dead-img" aria-disabled="true"><img src="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/images/donahue.gif" width="120" height="60" border="0"></a><br>
                <b>[ <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/tellafriend.asp" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">TELL 
                A FRIEND</a> ] [ <a href="http://www.msnbc.com/tools/newstools/e/emailextra.asp?nfeature=26&amp;0ct=-34w" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">Sign 
                up to the Donahue Daily Update</a> ]</b> </font></div>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="2"> 
              <hr height="1">
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="214"> 
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b>PMWATCH 
                - JULY 17, 2002</b> -- In the midst of the vast morass of hardline, 
                extremist, hatemongering, pro-occupation propaganda, whether blatantly 
                exhibited by <a href="http://www.foxnws.com" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">FoxNews</a> or barely 
                concealed by a thin veil (<a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/cnnbias5.asp">and the veil 
                is disappearing</a>) of "objectivity" and "balance" by <a href="http://www.cnn.com" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">CNN</a>, 
                a new island of sanity and common sense about the Palestinian-Israeli 
                conflict has somehow managed to emerge: <a href="http://www.msnbc.com/news/donahue_front.asp" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">Donahue</a>! 
                </font> 
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Just this 
                evening (July 17, 2002), for instance, <a href="http://www.msnbc.com/news/donahue_front.asp" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">Donahue</a> 
                ran an amazing segment -- truly a first in prime time American 
                Cable TV. While <a href="http://www.cnn.com" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">CNN</a> and <a href="http://www.foxnws.com" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">FoxNews</a> 
                were going through their usual script, where the usual suspects 
                are given extended stretches of time to spew their usual blinding 
                and numbing dehumanization of Palestinians, here was <a href="http://www.msnbc.com/news/donahue_front.asp" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">Donahue</a> 
                bringing two kids from <a href="http://www.seedsofpeace.org/" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">Seeds 
                of Peace</a> -- one Arab and the other Jewish -- to talk about 
                humanizing each other and building the future. A particularly 
                interesting moment was <a href="http://www.msnbc.com/news/donahue_front.asp" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">Donahue</a> 
                taking a much deserved jab at <a href="http://www.nytimes.com" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">The 
                New York Times</a> for not covering the coffins exhibition: Palestinian 
                and Israeli coffins lined up by Palestinian and Israeli families 
                in New York City - the very hometown of the <a href="http://www.nytimes.com" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">The 
                New York Times</a>. An impressive sight from the images <a href="http://www.msnbc.com/news/donahue_front.asp" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">Donahue</a> 
                showed. (This is the first we heard of it, by the way -- just 
                to show you the breakthrough in the mainstream media <a href="http://www.msnbc.com/news/donahue_front.asp" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">Donahue</a> 
                is!) </font> 
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> <a href="http://www.msnbc.com/news/donahue_front.asp" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">Donahue</a> 
                is doing something extremely important: he is injecting much needed 
                sanity in the mainstream debate about the Palestinian-Israeli 
                conflict, and is doing it WITHOUT APLOGIES! This is something 
                no other show has dared to do in any half-serious way, let alone 
                do it openly and with passion for the truth and a committed humanizing 
                compassion to all sides of this tragic conflict.</font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">And so, the 
                show is sure to be deluged with vicious attacks and <a href="http://www.msnbc.com/news/donahue_front.asp" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">Donahue</a> 
                is sure to be demonized and branded a "terrorist-lover" 
                and an "anti-Semite".</font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Please drop 
                <a href="http://www.msnbc.com/news/donahue_front.asp" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">Donahue</a> 
                a supportive note whenever you can, and every day, if you can 
                spare the minute or two. You can do that easily by entering your 
                letter below and hitting the "send" button. Don't delay!</font> 
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Your comments 
                will be sent to: </font> 
              </p><ul>
                <li><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Donahue@msnbc.com 
                  </font></li>
                <li><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">ombudsman@msnbc.com 
                  </font></li>
              </ul>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">And as importantly, 
                watch the show if you can spare the time, and encourage others 
                to do likewise.</font> 
              </p><p> <font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Palestine 
                Media Watch <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/index.html" class="dead" aria-disabled="true"><br>
                http://www.pmwatch.org</a><br>
                (610) 993 - 0608<br>
                Help keep PMWatch afloat -- donate via: <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/donations/index.html">http://www.pmwatch.org/pmw/donations/</a></font> 
            </p></td>
          </tr>
